traces.inference_trace:
Approach: strip the outer parentheses, try every split of the digits into a left and right part, and pair every valid number form of each side.

For a digit string `p`, the valid ways to write it as a number are:

- **As an integer (no decimal point):** allowed if `p` is a single digit, or if it does not start with `'0'`.
- **With a decimal point after position `i` (for `i` from 1 to `len-1`):** split into integer part `p[0..i)` and fractional part `p[i..)`.
  - The integer part must be `"0"` or must not start with `'0'`.
  - The fractional part must not end with `'0'`.

Each valid left form is combined with each valid right form as `"(L, R)"`. The string is at most 10 digits, so trying every split and every decimal position is cheap.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @return String[]
     */
    function ambiguousCoordinates($s) {
        $d = substr($s, 1, strlen($s) - 2);
        $n = strlen($d);
        $res = [];
        for ($k = 1; $k < $n; $k++) {
            $L = $this->gen(substr($d, 0, $k));
            if (empty($L)) continue;
            $R = $this->gen(substr($d, $k));
            foreach ($L as $a) {
                foreach ($R as $b) {
                    $res[] = "(" . $a . ", " . $b . ")";
                }
            }
        }
        return $res;
    }

    private function gen($p) {
        $out = [];
        $len = strlen($p);
        if ($len == 1 || $p[0] != '0') $out[] = $p;
        if ($p[$len - 1] == '0') return $out;
        for ($i = 1; $i < $len; $i++) {
            $ip = substr($p, 0, $i);
            if ($i > 1 && $ip[0] == '0') break;
            $out[] = $ip . "." . substr($p, $i);
        }
        return $out;
    }
}
```

