traces.inference_trace:
Count how often each character appears, then check that all the counts are the same.

1. `count_chars($s, 1)` returns an array of byte value → count, including only the characters that actually occur in `s`.
2. `array_unique` on those counts removes duplicates.
3. If exactly one distinct count remains, every character has the same frequency, so `s` is good.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function areOccurrencesEqual($s) {
        $counts = count_chars($s, 1);
        return count(array_unique($counts)) === 1;
    }
}
```

