traces.inference_trace:
Take the first two points as the reference line, with direction `(dx, dy) = (x1 - x0, y1 - y0)`.

Every other point `(x, y)` lies on that line exactly when the cross product of `(dx, dy)` and `(x - x0, y - y0)` is zero:

`dx * (y - y0) - dy * (x - x0) == 0`

This avoids division, so vertical lines need no special case.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[][] $coordinates
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function checkStraightLine($coordinates) {
        $x0 = $coordinates[0][0];
        $y0 = $coordinates[0][1];
        $dx = $coordinates[1][0] - $x0;
        $dy = $coordinates[1][1] - $y0;
        $n = count($coordinates);
        for ($i = 2; $i < $n; $i++) {
            $x = $coordinates[$i][0] - $x0;
            $y = $coordinates[$i][1] - $y0;
            if ($dx * $y - $dy * $x != 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

