traces.inference_trace:
Simulate the expression with a stack, applying operators in the fixed rotation `*`, `/`, `+`, `-`.

1. Push `n` onto the stack.
2. For each next number `i = n-1` down to `1`, use operator index `k % 4`:
   - **`*`**: pop the top value and push `top * i`.
   - **`/`**: pop the top value and push `intdiv(top, i)`. All values in the multiply/divide chain are non-negative, so truncation equals floor division.
   - **`+`**: push `i`.
   - **`-`**: push `-i`.
3. Return the sum of the stack.

Multiplications and divisions only ever touch the top of the stack, while additions and subtractions start new terms. This gives the correct order of operations.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @return Integer
     */
    function clumsy($n) {
        $stack = [$n];
        $k = 0;
        for ($i = $n - 1; $i >= 1; $i--) {
            $op = $k % 4;
            if ($op == 0) {
                $t = array_pop($stack);
                $stack[] = $t * $i;
            } elseif ($op == 1) {
                $t = array_pop($stack);
                $stack[] = intdiv($t, $i);
            } elseif ($op == 2) {
                $stack[] = $i;
            } else {
                $stack[] = -$i;
            }
            $k++;
        }
        return array_sum($stack);
    }
}
```

