traces.inference_trace:
Use lazy increments so every operation runs in O(1):

- Keep the values in a `stack` array, plus an `inc` array of the same length.
- **increment(k, val):** add `val` to `inc` at index `min(k, size) - 1`. Do nothing if the stack is empty.
- **pop():** take the top element at index `i` and return `stack[i] + inc[i]`. Before removing it, add `inc[i]` to `inc[i-1]` (if `i > 0`) so the pending increment carries down to the elements below.
- **push(x):** append `x` with an `inc` of 0, but only if the stack has not reached `maxSize`.

```php
class CustomStack {
    private $max;
    private $stack = [];
    private $inc = [];

    /**
     * @param Integer $maxSize
     */
    function __construct($maxSize) {
        $this->max = $maxSize;
        $this->stack = [];
        $this->inc = [];
    }

    /**
     * @param Integer $x
     * @return NULL
     */
    function push($x) {
        if (count($this->stack) < $this->max) {
            $this->stack[] = $x;
            $this->inc[] = 0;
        }
        return null;
    }

    /**
     * @return Integer
     */
    function pop() {
        $n = count($this->stack);
        if ($n == 0) return -1;
        $i = $n - 1;
        $res = $this->stack[$i] + $this->inc[$i];
        if ($i > 0) {
            $this->inc[$i - 1] += $this->inc[$i];
        }
        array_pop($this->stack);
        array_pop($this->inc);
        return $res;
    }

    /**
     * @param Integer $k
     * @param Integer $val
     * @return NULL
     */
    function increment($k, $val) {
        $n = count($this->stack);
        if ($n == 0) return null;
        $i = min($k, $n) - 1;
        $this->inc[$i] += $val;
        return null;
    }
}
```

