Use a greedy two-pointer approach. Keep `lo = 0` and `hi = n`, where `n` is the length of `s`.

1. Scan `s` from left to right.
2. On `'I'`, output `lo` and then increment it. Every later value is larger than `lo`, so `perm[i] < perm[i + 1]` holds whatever comes next.
3. On `'D'`, output `hi` and then decrement it. Every later value is smaller than `hi`, so `perm[i] > perm[i + 1]` holds.
4. After the scan, `lo == hi`. Append that last remaining value.

This runs in O(n) time and uses every integer in `[0, n]` exactly once.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @return Integer[]
     */
    function diStringMatch($s) {
        $n = strlen($s);
        $lo = 0;
        $hi = $n;
        $res = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            if ($s[$i] === 'I') {
                $res[] = $lo++;
            } else {
                $res[] = $hi--;
            }
        }
        $res[] = $lo;
        return $res;
    }
}
```

