Use a bitmask DP over rows.

**Valid masks for one row.** For each row, a mask is valid if:
- every chosen bit is on a good seat, i.e. `(mask & avail) == mask`;
- no two chosen seats are adjacent, i.e. `(mask & (mask << 1)) == 0`.

**Transition between rows.** Let `prev` be the previous row's mask and `cur` the current row's mask. They are compatible if no diagonal pair is occupied:
- `(cur & (prev << 1)) == 0`
- `(cur & (prev >> 1)) == 0`

Shifts can go past `n` bits, but that is harmless because `cur` only has its low `n` bits set.

**Complexity.** There are at most 256 masks per row, so each row transition costs at most 256 × 256 checks. Over 8 rows that is about 500k operations, which is fine. To reduce work, valid masks for each row are precomputed together with their popcounts.

**Seat parsing.** Seats may contain trailing spaces (as shown in the examples), so each cell is trimmed before checking whether it is `'.'`.

**DP.** `dp[mask]` is the best total ending with that mask in the current row. Initialize with `dp[0] = 0` for a virtual row before the first one. The answer is the maximum value in `dp` after the last row.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String[][] $seats
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maxStudents($seats) {
        $m = count($seats);
        $n = count($seats[0]);
        $dp = [0 => 0];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $m; $i++) {
            $avail = 0;
            for ($j = 0; $j < $n; $j++) {
                if (trim($seats[$i][$j]) === '.') $avail |= (1 << $j);
            }
            $valid = [];
            for ($mask = 0; $mask < (1 << $n); $mask++) {
                if (($mask & $avail) != $mask) continue;
                if ($mask & ($mask << 1)) continue;
                $c = 0; $x = $mask;
                while ($x) { $c += $x & 1; $x >>= 1; }
                $valid[$mask] = $c;
            }
            $ndp = [];
            foreach ($valid as $cur => $c) {
                $best = -1;
                foreach ($dp as $prev => $v) {
                    if (($cur & ($prev << 1)) || ($cur & ($prev >> 1))) continue;
                    if ($v > $best) $best = $v;
                }
                if ($best >= 0) $ndp[$cur] = $best + $c;
            }
            $dp = $ndp;
        }
        return max($dp);
    }
}
```

