Put the values of `nums` into a hash set so each membership check is O(1).

Walk the list once. A connected component ends at a node whose value is in the set when either:
- the next node is null, or
- the next node's value is not in the set.

Count each such ending node. That count is the number of components, found in O(n) time.

```php
/**
 * Definition for a singly-linked list.
 * class ListNode {
 *     public $val = 0;
 *     public $next = null;
 *     function __construct($val = 0, $next = null) {
 *         $this->val = $val;
 *         $this->next = $next;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param ListNode $head
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     * @return Integer
     */
    function numComponents($head, $nums) {
        $set = array_flip($nums);
        $count = 0;
        $cur = $head;
        while ($cur !== null) {
            if (isset($set[$cur->val]) && ($cur->next === null || !isset($set[$cur->next->val]))) {
                $count++;
            }
            $cur = $cur->next;
        }
        return $count;
    }
}
```

