Compare `s` against the alternating pattern that starts with `'0'` ("0101..."):

1. Walk through the string. At index `i`, the expected character is `'0'` when `i` is even and `'1'` when `i` is odd.
2. Count the mismatches; call this `cnt`.
3. The only other alternating string is "1010...". Every position that matches the first pattern mismatches the second, so it needs `n - cnt` changes.
4. The answer is `min(cnt, n - cnt)`.

The examples show trailing spaces in the input, so I only count `'0'` and `'1'` characters and skip anything else.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minOperations($s) {
        $n = strlen($s);
        $cnt = 0;
        $len = 0;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            $c = $s[$i];
            if ($c !== '0' && $c !== '1') continue;
            $expected = ($len % 2 == 0) ? '0' : '1';
            if ($c !== $expected) $cnt++;
            $len++;
        }
        return min($cnt, $len - $cnt);
    }
}
```

