Approach: precompute every pair's score, then run a bitmask DP over assigned mentors.

1. Let `m` be the number of students. Build `score[i][j]`, the number of matching answers between student `i` and mentor `j`.
2. Let `dp[mask]` be the best total score after assigning the first `popcount(mask)` students to exactly the mentors in `mask`.
3. Start with `dp[0] = 0` and every other entry at `-1` (unreachable).
4. For each reachable `mask`, the next student is `i = popcount(mask)`. For every mentor `j` not in `mask`, update `dp[mask | 1<<j]` with `dp[mask] + score[i][j]`.
5. The answer is `dp[(1<<m) - 1]`.

With `m ≤ 8` there are at most 256 masks, so the DP takes O(2^m · m) time, plus O(m² · n) for the scores.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[][] $students
     * @param Integer[][] $mentors
     * @return Integer
     */
    function maxCompatibilitySum($students, $mentors) {
        $m = count($students);
        $n = count($students[0]);
        $score = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $m; $i++) {
            for ($j = 0; $j < $m; $j++) {
                $s = 0;
                for ($k = 0; $k < $n; $k++) {
                    if ($students[$i][$k] == $mentors[$j][$k]) $s++;
                }
                $score[$i][$j] = $s;
            }
        }
        $full = 1 << $m;
        $dp = array_fill(0, $full, -1);
        $dp[0] = 0;
        for ($mask = 0; $mask < $full; $mask++) {
            if ($dp[$mask] < 0) continue;
            $i = 0;
            $x = $mask;
            while ($x) { $i += $x & 1; $x >>= 1; }
            if ($i >= $m) continue;
            for ($j = 0; $j < $m; $j++) {
                if (!($mask & (1 << $j))) {
                    $nm = $mask | (1 << $j);
                    $v = $dp[$mask] + $score[$i][$j];
                    if ($v > $dp[$nm]) $dp[$nm] = $v;
                }
            }
        }
        return $dp[$full - 1];
    }
}
```

