The idea is to count how many new operations must start at each position.

- At index 0, we need `target[0]` operations that begin there.
- At any later index `i`, operations that cover `i-1` can simply be extended to cover `i`. So if `target[i] <= target[i-1]`, no new operation is needed.
- If `target[i] > target[i-1]`, exactly `target[i] - target[i-1]` new operations must start at `i`.

So the answer is `target[0]` plus the sum of `max(0, target[i] - target[i-1])` over all `i >= 1`.

