Then take every pair of points `(x1, y1)` and `(x2, y2)` that can be opposite corners of a rectangle, meaning `x1 != x2` and `y1 != y2`. For such a pair, the other two corners are `(x1, y2)` and `(x2, y1)`. If both are in the set, the pair forms a rectangle with area `|x1 - x2| * |y1 - y2|`, and we keep the smallest one.

With n = 500 there are about 125k pairs, so the O(n²) check is fast enough. If no rectangle is found, return 0.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[][] $points
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minAreaRect($points) {
        $set = [];
        foreach ($points as $p) {
            $set[$p[0] * 40001 + $p[1]] = true;
        }
        $n = count($points);
        $best = PHP_INT_MAX;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            $x1 = $points[$i][0]; $y1 = $points[$i][1];
            for ($j = $i + 1; $j < $n; $j++) {
                $x2 = $points[$j][0]; $y2 = $points[$j][1];
                if ($x1 == $x2 || $y1 == $y2) continue;
                $area = abs($x1 - $x2) * abs($y1 - $y2);
                if ($area >= $best) continue;
                if (isset($set[$x1 * 40001 + $y2]) && isset($set[$x2 * 40001 + $y1])) {
                    $best = $area;
                }
            }
        }
        return $best == PHP_INT_MAX ? 0 : $best;
    }
}
```

