The approach is to convert each date into a day count from a fixed epoch (1971-01-01) and return the absolute difference of the two counts.

To compute the day count for a date:
1. For every full year from 1971 up to (but not including) the given year, add 365, plus 1 if that year is a leap year. A year is leap if it is divisible by 4 and not by 100, or divisible by 400.
2. Add the days of every full month before the given month in that year, counting February as 29 if the year is a leap year.
3. Add the day of the month.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $date1
     * @param String $date2
     * @return Integer
     */
    function daysBetweenDates($date1, $date2) {
        return abs($this->toDays($date1) - $this->toDays($date2));
    }

    private function isLeap($y) {
        return ($y % 4 == 0 && $y % 100 != 0) || $y % 400 == 0;
    }

    private function toDays($date) {
        $parts = explode('-', $date);
        $y = intval($parts[0]);
        $m = intval($parts[1]);
        $d = intval($parts[2]);
        $days = 0;
        for ($i = 1971; $i < $y; $i++) {
            $days += $this->isLeap($i) ? 366 : 365;
        }
        $md = [31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31];
        for ($i = 1; $i < $m; $i++) {
            $days += $md[$i - 1];
            if ($i == 2 && $this->isLeap($y)) $days += 1;
        }
        return $days + $d;
    }
}
```

