traces.inference_trace:
Scan left to right, matching each `]` against an earlier unmatched `[`:

- Keep `open`, the number of unmatched `[` seen so far.
- On `[`, increment `open`.
- On `]`, decrement `open` if it is positive; otherwise increment `unmatched`.

Once matched pairs are removed, what remains is `]]]...[[[`, with `unmatched` closing brackets in front. Each swap can fix two of these mismatches, so the answer is `ceil(unmatched / 2)`. Using integer arithmetic, that is `intdiv(unmatched + 1, 2)`.

The string can be up to 10^6 characters, so indexing `$s[$i]` directly in a loop is fine in PHP.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s
     * @return Integer
     */
    function minSwaps($s) {
        $n = strlen($s);
        $open = 0;
        $unmatched = 0;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            if ($s[$i] === '[') {
                $open++;
            } else {
                if ($open > 0) $open--;
                else $unmatched++;
            }
        }
        return intdiv($unmatched + 1, 2);
    }
}
```

