traces.inference_trace:
Use a monotonic stack and traverse the array twice to handle the circular wrap.

1. Start with every answer set to `-1`.
2. Iterate `i` from `0` to `2n - 1`, using index `idx = i % n`.
3. While the stack is non-empty and `nums[stack top] < nums[idx]`, pop the top index and set its answer to `nums[idx]`.
4. Push `idx` onto the stack only on the first pass (`i < n`). The second pass only resolves elements whose next greater number comes after wrapping around.

Each index is pushed and popped at most once, so this runs in O(n) time with O(n) extra space.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     * @return Integer[]
     */
    function nextGreaterElements($nums) {
        $n = count($nums);
        $res = array_fill(0, $n, -1);
        $stack = [];
        for ($i = 0; $i < 2 * $n; $i++) {
            $idx = $i % $n;
            $v = $nums[$idx];
            while (!empty($stack) && $nums[end($stack)] < $v) {
                $res[array_pop($stack)] = $v;
            }
            if ($i < $n) {
                $stack[] = $idx;
            }
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

