If the string is empty, no steps are needed, so return 0. If the whole string is already a palindrome, it can be removed in one step, so return 1. Otherwise, the answer is 2: remove every `'a'` as one subsequence (all the same letter, so it is a palindrome), then remove every `'b'` the same way.

