Precompute a map from each value to the list of indices where it appears. Each `pick` call then returns a uniformly random element of that list in O(1).

The map is keyed by value. PHP converts integer keys correctly, so negative values work as keys.

```php
class Solution {
    private $map;

    /**
     * @param Integer[] $nums
     */
    function __construct($nums) {
        $this->map = [];
        foreach ($nums as $i => $v) {
            $this->map[$v][] = $i;
        }
    }

    /**
     * @param Integer $target
     * @return Integer
     */
    function pick($target) {
        $list = $this->map[$target];
        return $list[mt_rand(0, count($list) - 1)];
    }
}
```

