Split each cell into 4 triangles and union them with a disjoint-set structure.

**Triangle numbering** (per cell `(i, j)`): 0 = top, 1 = right, 2 = bottom, 3 = left. Triangle `k` of the cell has id `base + k`, where `base = 4*(i*n + j)`.

**Unions inside a cell:**
- `' '`: union all four triangles.
- `'/'`: the slash runs bottom-left to top-right. Union top with left (0–3) and right with bottom (1–2).
- `'\'`: the slash runs top-left to bottom-right. Union top with right (0–1) and bottom with left (2–3).

**Unions between neighbouring cells:**
- The bottom triangle of `(i, j)` touches the top triangle of `(i+1, j)`.
- The right triangle of `(i, j)` touches the left triangle of `(i, j+1)`.

The answer is the number of disjoint sets left after all unions.

Each row is read as a string. In PHP `$grid[$i][$j]` gives a single character, and the backslash character is written `'\\'`.

```php
class Solution {
    private $p;

    private function find($x) {
        while ($this->p[$x] != $x) {
            $this->p[$x] = $this->p[$this->p[$x]];
            $x = $this->p[$x];
        }
        return $x;
    }

    private function union($a, $b) {
        $ra = $this->find($a);
        $rb = $this->find($b);
        if ($ra != $rb) {
            $this->p[$ra] = $rb;
            return 1;
        }
        return 0;
    }

    /**
     * @param String[] $grid
     * @return Integer
     */
    function regionsBySlashes($grid) {
        $n = count($grid);
        $total = 4 * $n * $n;
        $this->p = range(0, $total - 1);
        $count = $total;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            for ($j = 0; $j < $n; $j++) {
                $b = 4 * ($i * $n + $j);
                $c = $grid[$i][$j];
                if ($c == '/') {
                    $count -= $this->union($b, $b + 3);
                    $count -= $this->union($b + 1, $b + 2);
                } elseif ($c == '\\') {
                    $count -= $this->union($b, $b + 1);
                    $count -= $this->union($b + 2, $b + 3);
                } else {
                    $count -= $this->union($b, $b + 1);
                    $count -= $this->union($b + 1, $b + 2);
                    $count -= $this->union($b + 2, $b + 3);
                }
                if ($i + 1 < $n) {
                    $nb = 4 * (($i + 1) * $n + $j);
                    $count -= $this->union($b + 2, $nb);
                }
                if ($j + 1 < $n) {
                    $nb = 4 * ($i * $n + $j + 1);
                    $count -= $this->union($b + 1, $nb + 3);
                }
            }
        }
        return $count;
    }
}
```

