Sort the products lexicographically. Then, for each prefix of `searchWord`, binary-search for the first product that is `>=` the prefix. The suggestions are up to three products starting from that index that still begin with the prefix.

Details:
- `sort($products, SORT_STRING)` gives byte-wise order, which is the same as lexicographic order for lowercase letters.
- The lower bound only moves forward as the prefix grows, so the search for each new prefix can start from the previous result.
- The prefix check uses `strncmp($products[$j], $prefix, $len) === 0`.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String[] $products
     * @param String $searchWord
     * @return String[][]
     */
    function suggestedProducts($products, $searchWord) {
        sort($products, SORT_STRING);
        $n = count($products);
        $res = [];
        $start = 0;
        $prefix = '';
        $m = strlen($searchWord);
        for ($i = 0; $i < $m; $i++) {
            $prefix .= $searchWord[$i];
            $len = $i + 1;
            $lo = $start; $hi = $n;
            while ($lo < $hi) {
                $mid = ($lo + $hi) >> 1;
                if (strcmp($products[$mid], $prefix) < 0) $lo = $mid + 1;
                else $hi = $mid;
            }
            $start = $lo;
            $cur = [];
            for ($j = $lo; $j < $n && $j < $lo + 3; $j++) {
                if (strncmp($products[$j], $prefix, $len) === 0) $cur[] = $products[$j];
                else break;
            }
            $res[] = $cur;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
```

