Concatenate both sentences and count how often each word appears. A word is uncommon exactly when its total count across both sentences is 1.

Note on PHP: keys that look like numbers would be cast to integers in array keys. That can't happen here because words contain only lowercase letters. Still, casting each key back to `(string)` when building the result is a cheap safeguard.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param String $s1
     * @param String $s2
     * @return String[]
     */
    function uncommonFromSentences($s1, $s2) {
        $count = [];
        foreach (explode(' ', $s1 . ' ' . $s2) as $w) {
            if ($w === '') continue;
            if (!isset($count[$w])) $count[$w] = 0;
            $count[$w]++;
        }
        $res = [];
        foreach ($count as $w => $c) {
            if ($c == 1) $res[] = (string)$w;
        }
        return $res;
    }
}
