Greedy approach: build the string one character at a time.

- If the last two characters are the same letter, we must write the other letter next.
- Otherwise, write whichever letter has more remaining (ties go to `'a'`).

Because a valid answer is guaranteed to exist, this greedy choice never gets stuck.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $a
     * @param Integer $b
     * @return String
     */
    function strWithout3a3b($a, $b) {
        $s = '';
        $n = 0;
        while ($a > 0 || $b > 0) {
            $writeA = false;
            if ($n >= 2 && $s[$n-1] == $s[$n-2]) {
                $writeA = ($s[$n-1] == 'b');
            } else {
                $writeA = ($a >= $b);
            }
            if ($writeA) {
                $s .= 'a';
                $a--;
            } else {
                $s .= 'b';
                $b--;
            }
            $n++;
        }
        return $s;
    }
}
