traces.inference_trace:
Approach: a valid binary tree has exactly one root, every other node has exactly one parent, and every node is reachable from the root.

1. Count the in-degree of each node from `leftChild` and `rightChild`. If any node has more than one parent, return false.
2. Find the nodes with in-degree 0. There must be exactly one; that node is the root.
3. Run a BFS from the root, counting visited nodes and using a visited array to guard against cycles.
4. Return true only if the BFS visits exactly `n` nodes. This rules out cycles that sit apart from the root's component.

```php
class Solution {

    /**
     * @param Integer $n
     * @param Integer[] $leftChild
     * @param Integer[] $rightChild
     * @return Boolean
     */
    function validateBinaryTreeNodes($n, $leftChild, $rightChild) {
        $indeg = array_fill(0, $n, 0);
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            if ($leftChild[$i] != -1) {
                if (++$indeg[$leftChild[$i]] > 1) return false;
            }
            if ($rightChild[$i] != -1) {
                if (++$indeg[$rightChild[$i]] > 1) return false;
            }
        }
        $root = -1;
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            if ($indeg[$i] == 0) {
                if ($root != -1) return false;
                $root = $i;
            }
        }
        if ($root == -1) return false;
        $visited = array_fill(0, $n, false);
        $queue = [$root];
        $visited[$root] = true;
        $count = 0;
        $head = 0;
        while ($head < count($queue)) {
            $u = $queue[$head++];
            $count++;
            foreach ([$leftChild[$u], $rightChild[$u]] as $c) {
                if ($c != -1) {
                    if ($visited[$c]) return false;
                    $visited[$c] = true;
                    $queue[] = $c;
                }
            }
        }
        return $count == $n;
    }
}
```

